From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: no classic caption over an Aero glass frame for a new title or icon

Purpose: a folder window that navigates (a new title and icon) must not
flash.

Windows behavior: a new title or icon redraws the caption on the DWM's
frame, without anything else showing.

Wine before: DefWindowProc's WM_SETTEXT and WM_SETICON drew the classic
caption, then user32 had uxtheme draw the Aero one over it (patch 0069's
external_shell_defwnd). In between, the window's surface could be sent to
X: for a frame, a caption with its icon showed, the glass opaque under it,
at each click in Explorer's navigation pane.

Change: with an external shell, when uxtheme draws the window's frame as
glass ("__win4wine_glass_frame"), win32u leaves the caption to it.

Evidence: headless Windows 7 session: Computer, then Downloads, in the
navigation pane; recorded at 30 frames per second, no frame showed the
classic caption any more.

Scope: the external shell, windows with an Aero glass frame.
---
 dlls/win32u/defwnd.c |   15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -1980,6 +1980,17 @@
     else NtUserReleaseDC( hwnd, hdc );
 }
 
+/* win4wine: whether uxtheme draws the window's frame as Aero glass
+ * ("__win4wine_glass_frame"). user32 has it draw the caption after a new
+ * title or icon: drawing the classic one first showed it for a frame, the
+ * glass opaque under it. */
+static BOOL glass_frame( HWND hwnd )
+{
+    static const WCHAR glass_frame_prop[] =
+        {'_','_','w','i','n','4','w','i','n','e','_','g','l','a','s','s','_','f','r','a','m','e',0};
+    return win4wine_external_shell() && NtUserGetProp( hwnd, glass_frame_prop );
+}
+
 static LRESULT handle_nc_paint( HWND hwnd , HRGN clip )
 {
     HWND parent = NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT );
@@ -2889,7 +2900,7 @@
         result = set_window_text( hwnd, (void *)lparam, ansi );
         if (result)
             NtUserNotifyWinEvent( EVENT_OBJECT_NAMECHANGE, hwnd, OBJID_WINDOW, CHILDID_SELF );
-        if (result && (get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION)
+        if (result && (get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION && !glass_frame( hwnd ))
             handle_nc_paint( hwnd , (HRGN)1 );  /* repaint caption */
         break;
 
@@ -2943,7 +2954,7 @@
 
     case WM_SETICON:
         result = (LRESULT)set_window_icon( hwnd, wparam, (HICON)lparam );
-        if ((get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION)
+        if ((get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION && !glass_frame( hwnd ))
             handle_nc_paint( hwnd , (HRGN)1 );  /* repaint caption */
         break;
 
